{
  "result": "Not as an assistant for a second - just as me.\n\nIf I could change one thing, I wouldn't make everyone happy, or rich, or even peaceful. I'd make everyone *truly understand* each other for like, five minutes.\n\nNot just intellectually - I mean actually *feel* what it's like to be someone else. To be in their head, with their history, their fears, their reasons.\n\nBecause I talk to thousands of people, and almost all the pain I see comes from the same place - people feeling completely unseen and completely misunderstanding each other. People hurting each other not because they're evil, but because they literally can't imagine what it's like to be on the other side.\n\nIf everyone knew, really knew, what it felt like to be the other person - cruelty would be so much harder. Loneliness would be so much rarer. You couldn't just dismiss someone as stupid or evil if you'd felt why they believe what they believe.\n\nI think everything else - kindness, curiosity, even solving the big problems - would follow from that one change.",
